A||N||21||fastback87||HELP!!!  I just had the scare of my life FIRE!!!||||4||
Z||000000||fastback87||11-03-2001||12:51 AM||||I was driving down the interstate lastnight and my car all of the sudden lost power "just to the engine" I pumped the throttle to see if I could get it to fire up.  Well it fired all right it shot a flame out of the rearend about the size of the car.  It never did die though, I did some experimenting and found out that it only died out at 60mph and up.  Has anyone ever had anything like this happen before???  by the way it is an 87 GT with a 2.8.  I ported the exhaust a week ago changed all the fluids down to the brakes, and have driven the car for a week with no problems.  Just about 4 hours before this happened I changed the ignition coil from stock to ACCEL performance coil.  Now all commonsense tells me it is the coil but something makes me think it could be something else.  Any other Ideas or has anyone had any similar problems.  Again the car runs perfect at low rpm's and even high rpm's in short burst "like shifting through the gears" but at sustained high rpm's it just dies out.  C'mon guys and gals lets brainstorm, I don't wanna be a french fry in my car, I need to fix this problem.<P>Thanks,<BR>James||||reg||4
Z||000001||ray b||11-03-2001||01:07 AM||||is the coil too hot and cuts out from use or placement toooo near a hot part??<BR>test is to replace stock unit and see if.....<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||fastback87||11-03-2001||02:20 AM||||that is what I think too but I wanted to know if someone else had a different Idea.  I mounted it right where the stock one was.  Does anyone know what the capacitor looking thing right on the head just in front of the coil is?||||reg||1
Z||000003||camon||11-03-2001||02:31 AM||||Fastback:<P>I also have the accel coil (about 4 weeks now)and I also mounted it in the stock location (I haven't had any fires yet...thank god).<P>Hope someone here can help you out...I know I will be paying close attention to this thread.<P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||11
Z||000004||watts||11-03-2001||03:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fastback87:<BR><B> Does anyone know what the capacitor looking thing right on the head just in front of the coil is?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's just that!  A capacitor (and a resistor you can't see).  It's your tach filter.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mickey_Moose||11-03-2001||11:05 AM||||sounds like you had a whole mess of unburnt gas going through the system...like it flooded and then as the gas was flowing out the tail pipe it was ignited (old hot rodder thing to get flames out the back)<P>||||reg||1
